<title>CANADA: Canadian foreign reserves rise in Aug.</title>
<headline>Canadian foreign reserves rise in Aug.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian foreign reserve holdings rose during August, the Finance Department said on Thursday.</p>
<p>   RESERVES			  Aug 96     July 96</p>
<p>   Total			   19.603 bln  18.691 bln</p>
<p>   U.S. dollars		  16.505 bln  15.586 bln</p>
<p>   Other foreign currencies     508 million     520 million</p>
<p>   Gold				 160 million     161 million</p>
<p>   Special drawing rights     1.176 bln   1.175 bln</p>
<p>   IMF reserves		   1.254 bln   1.249 bln</p>
<p>Note - Figures in U.S. dollars.  </p>
<p>Official government operations decreased reserves by US$67 million.</p>
<p>Details of the changes in the month:</p>
<p>    Gain on gold sales		   + 3</p>
<p>    Earnings on investments	   + 89</p>
<p>    Revaluation effects		 - 20</p>
<p>    Foreign currency debt	    + 909</p>
<p>    Other transactions		   - 2</p>
<p>NOTE - in millions of U.S. dollars  </p>
<p>During August, Canada bills decreased by $91.0 million to a level of outstanding bills of $4.995 billion. A 10-year global bond was issued to raise $1.0 billion.</p>
<p>A Reuters survey of economists had predicted a rise in foreign reserves to $19.1 billion.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745</p>
